## SEVERITY / VERDICT (decided HERE)
*Blocker:* any request outside the exact three operations (or the page) that reaches the upstream as `admin`, or the page for a no-session visitor outside `/admin/feedback/review`; a path the door opens that the API serves as a different route; any change to Entra or `off` behaviour, to `needsSignIn` for any other path, to the API's Admin policy, or to a closed surface's answer for any visitor; a cross-site or wrong-Origin write that reaches the upstream; `.Destructive()` removed from any route but deleteFeedback; a path outside the lane with changed behaviour; a word, element, setting, header or environment variable added; lint, typecheck, build, `audit-dev`, `check-shards` red; a shard or API test red from the head; a hosted job projected over 1200 s; a secret; a non-ASCII byte or a person's name in an added line or the message. *Major:* a plant that stays green in both the builder's cells and your matrix; a hosted job projected over 960 s (alone or combined); a font- or layout-derived pixel literal that is not a same-run property; a claim in the builder's STATUS or the PR text that your numbers contradict; the browser cells hiding a BFF refusal; HEAD/PATCH/OPTIONS reaching a door route as admin. *Minor:* a false comment (`reviewDoor.ts:4`); a missing test for a measured-safe shape. *Note:* SQL Server NOT RUN (landing condition); NO PR, hosted CI and CodeQL NOT RUN; Chromium only; the UAT/demo copies not touched; anyone who can reach the UAT URL can read, approve and delete (the ruling). **GO** = steps 0-11 measured, nothing above Note; **GO WITH FINDINGS** = Minor/Note only; **NO GO** on any Blocker or Major.

